============================================

The person who associated a work with this deed has dedicated the work to the
public domain by waiving all of his or her rights to the work worldwide under
copyright law, including all related and neighboring rights, to the extent
allowed by law.

You can copy, modify, distribute and perform the work, even for commercial
purposes, all without asking permission.

Full text: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scope, and what is NOT covered
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This dedication covers the contents of this repository: the reference
implementations, the tools, the case manifests, the generated golden-vector
data files, the two probes, and the TLA+ specifications.

It does NOT cover, and this repository does not contain:

  * The sparse matrices themselves. Those come from the SuiteSparse Matrix
    Collection and carry their own terms. This repository ships only their
    provenance -- group, name, URL and sha256 -- and a script that fetches them.

  * Any compiled operator artifact. None is shipped. A serialized operator is a
    verbatim dump of an internal index and is not part of this release; the
    cases reference public matrices instead, which is also what makes them
    checkable by someone with no access to any of our software.

  * Any product runtime. Nothing here links against, embeds, or reproduces one.
